{
  "_comment": [
    "=== Pokemon Pinball+ Audio Configuration ===",
    "",
    "This file controls which music and SFX play for each game event.",
    "",
    "=== Custom audio files (WAV/OGG) ===",
    "Add a 'file' field to any music or SFX entry to replace the GBC",
    "bytecode track with your own audio file. Supported formats:",
    "  - WAV (.wav) — any sample rate/channels, auto-converted",
    "  - OGG Vorbis (.ogg) — decoded via stb_vorbis",
    "File paths are relative to the asset base path (project root).",
    "",
    "Example: { \"bank\": 15, \"id\": 1, \"file\": \"audio/custom/my_music.ogg\" }",
    "",
    "Custom music loops automatically. Custom SFX plays once.",
    "If the file is missing or fails to load, falls back to bytecode.",
    "The bank/id still serves as the fallback track.",
    "",
    "=== How bank/id works ===",
    "Each song or sound effect is identified by a (bank, id) pair.",
    "There are 5 audio banks (15-19 = 0x0F-0x13), each containing",
    "its own set of music tracks, SFX, drum kits, and Pokemon cries.",
    "The 'id' selects which track within that bank to play.",
    "",
    "=== Remapping existing audio ===",
    "You can swap any music or SFX to a different game event by",
    "changing its bank/id to point to another existing track.",
    "For example, to play the Blue Field music on the title screen,",
    "change title_screen to { \"bank\": 16, \"id\": 1 }.",
    "",
    "=== Pikachu voice clips ===",
    "The pikachu_clips section lets you replace the two Pikachu voice clips.",
    "Supports WAV and OGG. Paths are relative to the asset base path.",
    "Omit the section or leave paths empty to use the original WAV files.",
    "",
    "=== Volume ===",
    "master: 0-200 (percentage). Controls overall output volume.",
    "music:  0-200 (percentage). Controls custom music file volume.",
    "sfx:    0-200 (percentage). Controls custom SFX file volume.",
    "Omit any field to use its default (100%).",
    "Tip: custom WAV/OGG files are often much louder than the GBC",
    "bytecode audio. Set music to 30-50 for a good balance."
  ],

